/P 83 0 R
/E (PART 2 - Integrating established teaching methodologies in robotics and coding)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Educational robotics and coding are rapidly becoming integral parts of modern education, fostering essential skills such as critical thinking, problem-solving, and creativity. To effectively teach these subjects, educators can leverage a variety of well-known teaching methodologies. Each of these methodologies offers unique advantages and can be adapted to enhance the learning experience in robotics and coding. This section explores several prominent teaching methodologies and how they can be applied to educational robotics and coding to create an engaging and effective learning environment.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Project-based learning \(PBL\))
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (It is a student-centered methodology that involves students working on a project over an extended period. In educational robotics, PBL can involve designing, building, and programming robots to solve real-world problems. This approach encourages critical thinking, creativity, and practical application of theoretical knowledge. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
endobj
