/P 86 0 R
/E (Collaborative Learning is an educational approach that emphasizes group work, shared goals, and collective responsibility for learning. In robotics and coding, it is particularly effective because these fields naturally involve problem-solving in teams, dividing tasks, and integrating different perspectives. In a collaborative learning environment, students are placed in small, diverse groups where they co-construct knowledge and negotiate solutions. A typical robotics project may assign roles such as engineer, coder, project manager, and documentarian, ensuring that each student contributes in a meaningful way while also learning from others. Key elements of effective collaborative learning in robotics include:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
