314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Learning boxes are inspired by challenge-based education and promote hands-on, project-oriented learning. Each learning box is centered around a specific challenge, integrating multiple subjects to provide a holistic educational experience. Tasks are scaffolded to increase in complexity, encouraging skill development and confidence. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Key features include collaborative learning, where students work in groups to enhance teamwork and communication skills, and reflective practice, allowing students to consider their learning process and apply new knowledge to different contexts. The implementation involves introducing the challenge, exploration and research, practical application, iteration and improvement, and presentation and reflection.  The learning boxes can connect robotics and coding to real-world challenges and boost student motivation and interest. For example, a learning box on climate change could include a "Rescue Robot Adventure" task where students design, build, and program a simple robot to navigate a pretend disaster area, locate objects, and deliver essential supplies.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
