/E (Example of a Learning box activity - Rescue Robot Adventure)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (A group of students is engaged in a learning box activity. The students are actively opening and examining the contents, which include instruction sheets, materials, tools, robot components and task cards. The box is climate change and includes several relevant tasks. One of the key tasks in the learning box is the Rescue Robot Adventure. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [20 21]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (The Rescue Robot Adventure involves designing, building, and programming a robot to rescue a character from a natural disaster, simulating a real-world rescue mission. The activity begins with an introduction to the challenge, through a scenario brief and discussion among students. Students then brainstorm ideas, sketch their robot designs, and select appropriate materials and tools from the learning box. Then, students assemble their robot, test their functionality, and make necessary adjustments. They write and debug the code to control the robot, ensuring it can detect obstacles and navigate the terrain effectively. The task includes trial runs to fine-tune the robot's performance. After the mission, students reflect on the challenges faced and the lessons learned. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [22 23]
>>
endobj
