/T (In a differentiated robotics and coding class, students might start with a common project brief, such as designing a robot to complete a specific task. Based on their skill levels, different groups might work on varying aspects of the project. Beginners could focus on assembling the robot and learning basic coding commands, while advanced students might tackle more complex programming challenges and optimize the robot's performance. Throughout the project, the teacher provides individualized support and resources tailored to each group's needs. By employing differentiated learning in educational robotics and coding, teachers can ensure that all students are challenged appropriately and supported in their learning journey. This approach not only caters to diverse learning needs but also fosters a more inclusive and engaging educational environment.)
/E (In a differentiated robotics and coding class, students might start with a common project brief, such as designing a robot to complete a specific task. Based on their skill levels, different groups might work on varying aspects of the project. Beginners could focus on assembling the robot and learning basic coding commands, while advanced students might tackle more complex programming challenges and optimize the robot's performance. Throughout the project, the teacher provides individualized support and resources tailored to each group's needs. By employing differentiated learning in educational robotics and coding, teachers can ensure that all students are challenged appropriately and supported in their learning journey. This approach not only caters to diverse learning needs but also fosters a more inclusive and engaging educational environment.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
endobj
