437 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 93 0 R
/T (In performing arts or language classes, students can use robots as animated puppets or theatrical characters. After writing short dialogues or scripts, students program robots to act out scenes with movement and voice. They may add costumes, backgrounds, or props to enrich the performance. For example, in a modern fairy tale project, each robot represents a character who interacts with others according to a programmed sequence of speech and motion. This format supports oral language skills, expressive movement, and team-based creativity.)
/E (In performing arts or language classes, students can use robots as animated puppets or theatrical characters. After writing short dialogues or scripts, students program robots to act out scenes with movement and voice. They may add costumes, backgrounds, or props to enrich the performance. For example, in a modern fairy tale project, each robot represents a character who interacts with others according to a programmed sequence of speech and motion. This format supports oral language skills, expressive movement, and team-based creativity.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
