/T (Robots can also be used in social studies, ethics, or philosophy classes to simulate moral dilemmas and encourage discussion. For example, students can design a scenario where a robot must choose between helping a friend or reaching a goal, with consequences triggered by its programmed path. After watching the outcome, students engage in guided reflection about values, choices, and social responsibility. This kind of experiential learning brings ethical thinking into action, fostering both empathy and critical reasoning.)
/E (Robots can also be used in social studies, ethics, or philosophy classes to simulate moral dilemmas and encourage discussion. For example, students can design a scenario where a robot must choose between helping a friend or reaching a goal, with consequences triggered by its programmed path. After watching the outcome, students engage in guided reflection about values, choices, and social responsibility. This kind of experiential learning brings ethical thinking into action, fostering both empathy and critical reasoning.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
